PWD(1)                         P32W Unix                          PWD(1)

NAME
       pwd - print the working directory name

SYNOPSIS
       pwd

DESCRIPTION
       pwd prints the full path name of the current directory,
       followed by a newline.

EXAMPLES
       pwd                           e.g. /usr/ken

EXIT STATUS
       0 on success; 1 if the name could not be found (for example
       it is longer than 255 characters), with a message.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1), ls(1), chdir(2)

BUGS
       Arguments are ignored. There are no -L or -P options.
